---
import WasmShowcase from "../../components/WasmShowcase.astro";
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>WebRev WASM Lab</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: dark;
        font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
        background: #030405;
        color: #f8f8f6;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(69,86,130,.18), transparent 42%),
          #030405;
      }

      main {
        width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px));
        margin: auto;
        padding: 82px 0 110px;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        letter-spacing: .2em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        opacity: .6;
        font-size: .72rem;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
        line-height: .94;
        letter-spacing: -.06em;
        margin: .2em 0;
        max-width: 930px;
      }

      .lede {
        max-width: 780px;
        color: #b8bdc7;
        line-height: 1.7;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <div class="eyebrow">WEBREV / WASM LAB</div>
      <h1>Throw it. Squash it. Swap the runtime.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This isolated graphics placement is intentionally simple enough to compare runtimes and expressive enough to expose real differences in input, motion, deformation, and frame behavior. It currently has a JavaScript fallback; a WASM module can take over the same placement contract later.
      </p>

      <WasmShowcase />
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
